<title>USA: Banco do Brasil to sell $400 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>Banco do Brasil to sell $400 mln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco do Brasil SA is expected to issue $400 million in five- and 10-year debt securities on Wednesday via lead manager UBS Securities, according to emerging market syndicate sources.</p>
<p>Rough price talk on the debt is 210 to 220 basis points over the U.S. Treasury curve for five-year notes and 270 to 280 basis points over the curve for 10-year paper, said one source not in the selling group.</p>
<p>The size of tranches was not available. UBS's syndicate desk declined comment on the deal.</p>
<p>The issue is a 144A private placement offering.</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bonds, 212-859-1672))</p>
</text>
